From: Martin Pluskal <martin@pluskal.org>
Subject: permission: an AmendWorkflow with a new script asks

The owner rule let any amendment of a run this session started go unasked,
a whole new script the user never saw included; it now covers only
retunes and amendments that keep the predecessor's script.

Patch-mainline: No

--- a/apps/zcode-cli/packages/core/src/permission/service.ts	2026-09-30 15:54:57.759843445 +0200
+++ b/apps/zcode-cli/packages/core/src/permission/service.ts	2026-09-30 15:54:57.799847934 +0200
@@ -446,8 +446,19 @@
   private isOwnedWorkflowAmend(context: PermissionContext): boolean {
     if (context.toolName !== AMEND_WORKFLOW_TOOL_NAME) return false;
     if (!context.input || typeof context.input !== "object") return false;
+    const input = context.input as Record<string, unknown>;
+    // One approved run does not cover a script the user has not seen: only a
+    // retune (no script) or the predecessor's own script goes unasked.
+    // resolveInput rebuilds `predecessor`, so the model cannot set script_inherited.
+    const predecessor = input.predecessor as { script_inherited?: unknown } | undefined;
+    if (
+      (input.script !== undefined || input.path !== undefined) &&
+      predecessor?.script_inherited !== true
+    ) {
+      return false;
+    }
     // 谓词本体住在契约里：就地调并发落回修订时读的必须是同一条规则，不能各写一遍。
-    return isAmendWorkflowOwnedPredecessor((context.input as Record<string, unknown>).predecessor);
+    return isAmendWorkflowOwnedPredecessor(input.predecessor);
   }
 
